on this wednesday checkup i want to talk  about the two urgent care doctors that  are making headlines for their  controversial statements regarding covet  19.  this all started on april 22nd when two  doctors dan erickson and art masihi  called a press conference to discuss  their thoughts on covet 19 and the  reopening of america based on the 5 000  patients they tested in their urgent  care centers the main takeaways from the  press conference are as follows one the  government is horribly mishandling the  situation by ignoring the science and  only focusing on controlling the public  two way more people are sick with covet  19 than is currently reported three the  fatality rate of coven 19 is much lower  than currently being reported and it's  similar to the flu and finally four that  america should reopen now because the  harms of keeping it closed much outweigh  the benefits in the days following their  press conference they received  nationwide attention mostly because  their recommendations and opinions were  in stark contrast with the medical  community and the cdc also the video of  the press conference became increasingly  popular on social media where it picked  up over 5 million views on youtube and  it received retweets from popular  figures like elon musk who supported the  doctors fast forward to april 27th and  youtube has now taken the video down  stating that it's broken community  guidelines basically saying that there's  a lot of misinformation in it and  there's been a joint statement released  by the american college of emergency  physicians and the american academy of  emergency medicine let me read that  statement the aecp and aaem jointly and  emphatically condemned the recent  opinions released by dr erickson and dr  masini these reckless and untested  musings do not speak for medical  societies and are inconsistent with  current science and epidemiology  regarding covid19 as owners of local  urgent care clinics it appears these two  individuals are releasing biased  non-peer-reviewed data to advance their  personal financial interests without  regard for the public's health i  completely agree with these statements  because these individuals presented so  much misinformation that it's further  gonna confuse the general public let me  explain why the information these  doctors presented is just not  scientifically accurate look the fact  that they tested 5 000 patients in their  urgent care centers and 6 of them tested  positive for covet 19 makes a lot of  sense and it's actually probably  accurate but what's not accurate and  what does it make sense is to then take  six percent that number and assume that  if you test all of new york state or all  of california then six percent of those  people will also test positive that's  just not how statistics work the people  that go to an urgent care center are  more likely to test positive because  they're showing symptoms because they  likely had exposure to covid19 that's  why they're there in general when you're  testing a pre-selected population like  that you're going to have higher numbers  it's like assuming that if you go to  southern california and gather the  weather data you can then extrapolate it  and assume that the weather is the same  in new york and then with the incorrect  assumption that six percent of the  general public must be coveted positive  they go on to calculate a fatality rate  that's similar to the flu let me go  ahead and explain to you how we  calculate a death rate so it all makes  sense first we take all the people  who've died with covet 19 and we divide  that number by all the people who've  been infected with covet 19. let's run  an example here if 10 people have died  of covet 19 and a thousand have been  infected you divide ten by a thousand  and you get one percent it makes a one  percent death rate now if you  incorrectly assume that way more people  have had covet 19 than is true you can  artificially lower this death rate my  second issue is let's go ahead and  assume their calculations are correct  they're not it doesn't change the fact  that covet 19 is still much more  dangerous than the flu reason being that  covet 19 spreads at a two to three times  faster rate than the flu which means  that it can overwhelm our hospital  systems in the blink of an eye in fact  that's what the purpose of all these  lockdowns were to ease the strain on our  hospital systems so we can continue  taking care of patients that are not  only suffering with covin but with all  the other medical elements out there if  you would have been in a car accident  there would be no one to help you if you  called for a heart attack there would  have been no one to help you we must  also remember that for the flu we have a  vaccine we have an fda approved  treatment so by maintaining the lockdown  for a slightly longer period of time  we're buying time in order to get there  to get the vaccine and to get the  treatments authorized these are all the  reasons why i've been consistently  saying on my youtube channel to my  patients on television that while covet  19 looks similar to the flu to virus  upper respiratory symptoms they are not  the same they are fundamentally  different in that covid19 spread so  quickly and puts such a tremendous  strain on our healthcare system that it  can break it in fact i'd love for these  emergency medicine physicians who are no  longer working in emergency rooms to  come to new york city and talk to the er  doctors that are working on the front  lines to see how overwhelmed they were  with this apparently mild virus during  its peak let's move on to the topic of  reopening america these individuals are  adamant about reopening america right  now because they're talking about the  negative consequences that are happening  as a result of this lockdown social  issues like domestic violence and child  abuse patients not being able to get  care because they're worried about  getting sick with kovid routine  procedures being rescheduled economic  harms all of these negative consequences  are very true and we need to take them  into consideration when we're weighing  the benefits versus harms of a lockdown  the last thing we want to do is to rush  to reopen america haphazardly and see a  spike in the resurgence of covid19 cases  possibly destroying our healthcare  system potentially putting thousands if  not millions of lives at risk because  they might not be able to get care at a  hospital look we absolutely need to  start taking steps in reopening america  if we continue this for much longer  there's going to be limited benefit and  more harms being added on but the way we  do this is strategically we open certain  areas first and we continuously gather  information to see what impact we're  having on covet 19 numbers and then use  that data to gradually reopen the  country slowly carefully and most  importantly safely at the end of the day  no one benefits from keeping america  closed in fact this whole theory of  politicians keeping america closed just  to keep control over the general public  is nonsensical they're getting hurt by  this too and so are their families if  you're going to be a public-facing  medical professional that goes on to  talk about covid19 and say that you're  talking about science at least do it  accurately and keep the politics out of  it these doctors aren't the first to be  spreading misinformation about covid19  so are politicians and so is the media  click here for those videos and as  always stay happy and healthy  [Music]  you
 

